{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/android/app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:50:09.005246Z","id":"1677fc18c0fbe974bd58d6bea3c94e03df5c1f66f0f0865d9e9afc015725528d","body":{"detail":"A SEND intent carries its file in EXTRA_STREAM, not in Intent.data. Android's intent-filter data test passes an intent with a MIME type and no URI only when the filter names no URI scheme, so adding <data android:scheme=\"content\"/> to this filter would stop every share from matching. The schemes are on the VIEW filter (lines 55-64) only.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":65},"end":{"line":71},"content_hash":"1de625c0e13e44e6cc318db17b00f83dc4449b20bd442170d552d09c01fa966e"},"summary":"SEND filter without the content/file scheme data elements that docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-13-flutter-app-bundles-design.md §12.2 lists","tags":["revisit:a device test shows shares of .clax files not reaching MainActivity","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/android/app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:54:19.801056Z","id":"dd8f978cd93e18cb9ea9cbec178bce009338fbb18d945e2e59d47bb64f011e97","body":{"detail":"Failure: open a .clax attachment in a mail or messaging app, or share one through the system share sheet, while those apps start the intent without FLAG_ACTIVITY_NEW_TASK (the usual case for VIEW of an attachment and for share targets). launchMode singleTop reuses an instance only when it is on top of the caller's own task, so Android creates a new MainActivity inside the sender's task: configureFlutterEngine runs again with a new engine, Dart main starts a second app (and its embedded daemon start) against the same home, BundleIntake's init (BundleIntake.kt:51) deletes <cache>/incoming/ under the first instance, and the second instance's onDestroy (MainActivity.kt:88-105) clears AppNoticeChannel and BackgroundRunService.onStopped for the first. docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-13-flutter-app-bundles-design.md section 12.2 (line 689) names singleTop, so the fix changes the spec: launchMode singleTask (taskAffinity=\"\" keeps it a task of its own), or a small exported trampoline activity (noHistory, translucent) that forwards the URI to MainActivity with FLAG_ACTIVITY_NEW_TASK | FLAG_ACTIVITY_SINGLE_TOP and FLAG_GRANT_READ_URI_PERMISSION. Follows Android's documented launchMode behaviour; not run on a device.","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":30},"end":{"line":38},"content_hash":"2a601581b48b86e408f5b2c75ad673f32036d66777ac34b80b969560d538c086"},"summary":"singleTop puts a second MainActivity, with its own FlutterEngine, in the sender's task when a file is opened or shared from another app","tags":["review","bp","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/android/app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:54:19.801272Z","id":"04017a42988770e5699cd62d9ec32c78db066dd2e149f71820fc8167cbd9bbab","body":{"detail":"IntentFilter.matchData in AOSP: when the filter lists schemes, the intent's scheme (\"\" for a SEND intent, whose Intent.data is null) must be among them or the match fails with NO_MATCH_DATA; a filter that lists only MIME types matches an intent with no data or with content:/file: data. So the SEND filter at lines 65-71 is right without schemes, and the explicit schemes on the VIEW filter (lines 59-60) are redundant but harmless. The merged manifest in build/app/outputs/flutter-apk/app-debug.apk (aapt2 dump xmltree --file AndroidManifest.xml) carries both filters as written. docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-13-flutter-app-bundles-design.md section 12.2 (lines 688-694) should drop the schemes from SEND.","kind":"comment","references":"1677fc18c0fbe974bd58d6bea3c94e03df5c1f66f0f0865d9e9afc015725528d","span":{"start":{"line":65},"end":{"line":71},"content_hash":"1de625c0e13e44e6cc318db17b00f83dc4449b20bd442170d552d09c01fa966e"},"summary":"Confirmed: a scheme on the SEND filter would stop shares from matching","tags":["review","bp","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/android/app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:57:23.186806Z","id":"21fa0cf21905dec0ae5e05dc0fdcef69c02867ed7097297b9dd66b89c4eb549a","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"dd8f978cd93e18cb9ea9cbec178bce009338fbb18d945e2e59d47bb64f011e97","summary":"Decided by the coordinator (the owner may overrule): MainActivity stays singleTop with only MAIN/LAUNCHER; the VIEW and SEND filters move to an exported, noHistory, translucent BundleReceiverActivity that forwards the content: URI with FLAG_GRANT_READ_URI_PERMISSION to MainActivity (NEW_TASK | SINGLE_TOP | CLEAR_TOP) and finishes. docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-13-flutter-app-bundles-design.md §12.2 says so (git:f1c07f346b12).","tags":["status:decided","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/android/app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:57:23.186891Z","id":"b9c601695b9c81582c240ba0269940e1c84fe4db61699abdf09d8db7f2c1c961","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed: the intake filters are on BundleReceiverActivity (BundleReceiverActivity.kt), which forwards to the one MainActivity in Clax's task. aapt2 dump xmltree of build/app/outputs/flutter-apk/app-debug.apk: MainActivity launchMode=1 with only MAIN/LAUNCHER; BundleReceiverActivity exported, noHistory, with the VIEW (content) and SEND filters. flutter build apk --debug: EXIT 0 (target/bp-apk-build2.log). Task reuse on a device is unexercised (record 7219cb27).","supersedes":"dd8f978cd93e18cb9ea9cbec178bce009338fbb18d945e2e59d47bb64f011e97","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/android/app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:57:23.188331Z","id":"0d645ff916867cf1ade2ce269a6e1d2b70ca9a46f54a965ad7366d0c25618d3e","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"The spec now names no scheme on SEND (§12.2, git:f1c07f346b12), so this is no longer a path not taken.","supersedes":"1677fc18c0fbe974bd58d6bea3c94e03df5c1f66f0f0865d9e9afc015725528d","tags":["reason:obsolete","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/android/app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T08:41:14.303535Z","id":"c8f2a42bcbf64a526de5e6d4370dcabbf45de2db709ccc9ff14b9f12289d2d2d","body":{"detail":"apps/clax_app/test/ui/app_screen_test.dart ('a predictive back gesture …' in 'back goes back in the app first') drives flutter/backgesture as the engine would, and //apps/clax_app:apk_test checks android:enableOnBackInvokedCallback in the built manifest. Untested on a device: the system back-to-home animation from the home screen, the in-page back over a WebView whose history.back is true (the route must not follow the finger), and the gesture with the keyboard up.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":24},"end":{"line":31},"content_hash":"3f21eb16b04f4f02b8e47dc4c7c255fd2be46c28000018d44625476449c5aaf9"},"summary":"Predictive back is verified in widget tests and apk_test only, not on an Android 13+ device","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/android/app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T18:17:18.004647Z","id":"33948a509d3b6dbb0435796d1635919fad131f82b9b1085f1ab63b67341069fd","body":{"detail":"The manifest no longer sets android:extractNativeLibs and build.gradle.kts no longer sets useLegacyPackaging. AGP then writes extractNativeLibs=false into the merged manifest and stores the libraries uncompressed; the Bazel APK (flutter_fat_apk) uses this manifest as written, so the platform default (extract) applies and apk_test shows lib/arm64-v8a/libclax_embed.so 37,448,280 bytes stored as 15,649,252. Both load with DynamicLibrary.open('libclax_embed.so'); the Bazel install takes the extracted copy's disk space and the APK download is smaller. Neither APK was run on a device or the emulator with the core.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":29},"end":{"line":35},"content_hash":"ddda2972b6daa54c6c60856dc2b28bbc98480c92e34e82f68c5369a0432420d6"},"summary":"With extractNativeLibs unset, the Bazel APK still stores libclax_embed.so compressed and extracts it at install, while a Gradle build stores it uncompressed and page-aligned","tags":["core","android","packaging","unverified","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/android/app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T22:27:54.228595Z","id":"23a229746c91fff05cc7daa5c913126959be9ce3db7db34083a15503333f88b3","body":{"detail":"The manifest no longer sets android:extractNativeLibs and build.gradle.kts no longer sets useLegacyPackaging. AGP then writes extractNativeLibs=false into the merged manifest and stores the libraries uncompressed; the Bazel APK (flutter_fat_apk) uses this manifest as written, so the platform default (extract) applies and apk_test shows lib/arm64-v8a/libclax_embed.so 37,448,280 bytes stored as 15,649,252. Both load with DynamicLibrary.open('libclax_embed.so'); the Bazel install takes the extracted copy's disk space and the APK download is smaller. Neither APK was run on a device or the emulator with the core.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":29},"end":{"line":34},"content_hash":"8255ce8978e9a6b64968c2149317b71929047e68a1fa83efc491125f32dfa9b4"},"summary":"With extractNativeLibs unset, the Bazel APK still stores libclax_embed.so compressed and extracts it at install, while a Gradle build stores it uncompressed and page-aligned","supersedes":"33948a509d3b6dbb0435796d1635919fad131f82b9b1085f1ab63b67341069fd","tags":["core","android","packaging","unverified","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/android/app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-21T02:46:16.741424Z","id":"0402bdadb0965ba4ebe7fa4598bc76e6028ccde7a799638a2d82a1a7c4ff0f62","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"23a229746c91fff05cc7daa5c913126959be9ce3db7db34083a15503333f88b3","summary":".bazelrc and docs/bazel.md no longer say the Bazel APK compresses its native libraries 'as Gradle does' (49a0cccabd27): they now say Gradle stores them uncompressed and page-aligned with extractNativeLibs=false, and only the Bazel APK compresses them. The manifest gained android:dataExtractionRules and android:fullBackupContent (f1c07f346b12), which moves this record's span.","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/android/app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T04:26:34.220534Z","id":"732411078090e6580cfff5b3d481a151983c8642184bbda8369600f2786efc03","body":{"detail":"minSdk is 29 (android/app/build.gradle.kts:23). On API 31+ Android sends an http(s) link whose domain is not verified for any app to the default browser without a chooser; only Android 10 and 11 show the chooser. Until assetlinks.json names the release key, phones on Android 12+ land on the /a/<id>/get web page, not Clax.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":100},"end":{"line":105},"content_hash":"65f74b88025325be95e75e8d50bade7d03d776064249a7827107fc57917c16ef"},"suggested_fix":"Say: unverified, Android 12+ opens it in the browser (10 and 11 ask which app).","summary":"The comment says an unverified clax.dev link makes Android ask which app opens it; from Android 12 an unverified web link opens in the browser","tags":["links","docs","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/android/app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T04:44:54.823644Z","id":"04975022ccb9897fc91651ad8d25c94ee8fde33a0c85f497aeac2f942ba548ba","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:b93c9676a","summary":"The comment above the clax.dev autoVerify filter now says Android 12 and later open an unverified link in the browser, and earlier versions ask which app opens it.","supersedes":"732411078090e6580cfff5b3d481a151983c8642184bbda8369600f2786efc03","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/android/app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:31:41.179388Z","id":"d8662ab0a52fc5c81499240b3634769ddd44a41f1b4e856b34ae135d19be22f8","body":{"detail":"apps/clax_app/test/ui/app_screen_test.dart ('a predictive back gesture …' in 'back goes back in the app first') drives flutter/backgesture as the engine would, and //apps/clax_app:apk_test checks android:enableOnBackInvokedCallback in the built manifest. Untested on a device: the system back-to-home animation from the home screen, the in-page back over a WebView whose history.back is true (the route must not follow the finger), and the gesture with the keyboard up.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae)'s record.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":24},"end":{"line":34},"content_hash":"ec2a93980abf5e6e871eb6d689497948917de3841767be225f9d0e0fbd2b193c"},"summary":"Predictive back is verified in widget tests and apk_test only, not on an Android 13+ device","supersedes":"c8f2a42bcbf64a526de5e6d4370dcabbf45de2db709ccc9ff14b9f12289d2d2d","tags":["session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/android/app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:31:41.280162Z","id":"c1674917b45f1e0e21bb06c08525c63c2e9fc2e44b68a9fc3c391a407b7f3b97","body":{"detail":"The manifest no longer sets android:extractNativeLibs and build.gradle.kts no longer sets useLegacyPackaging. AGP then writes extractNativeLibs=false into the merged manifest and stores the libraries uncompressed; the Bazel APK (flutter_fat_apk) uses this manifest as written, so the platform default (extract) applies and apk_test shows lib/arm64-v8a/libclax_embed.so 37,448,280 bytes stored as 15,649,252. Both load with DynamicLibrary.open('libclax_embed.so'); the Bazel install takes the extracted copy's disk space and the APK download is smaller. Neither APK was run on a device or the emulator with the core.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae)'s record.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":32},"end":{"line":39},"content_hash":"2b3a79267187cf57a51daa37e8fe762429781f1405a5b74e500889fe244e00e8"},"summary":"With extractNativeLibs unset, the Bazel APK still stores libclax_embed.so compressed and extracts it at install, while a Gradle build stores it uncompressed and page-aligned","supersedes":"23a229746c91fff05cc7daa5c913126959be9ce3db7db34083a15503333f88b3","tags":["core","android","packaging","unverified","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
